.TH RDP 1
.SH NAME
rdp \- remote debug protocol client over a serial line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rdp
.RB [ -crdlht ]
.RB [ -e\fIc\fR ]
.RB [ -O\fIofs\fR ]
.RB [ -p\fIport\fR ]
.RB [ -s\fIbps\fR ]
.RI [ prog ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rdp
talks a remote debug protocol to a target over a serial line (default
port
.BR /dev/eia0 ,
default speed 38400 bps), for loading and debugging a program on
embedded hardware that has no display of its own.
.I Prog,
if given, is the local image to load onto the target.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/rdp.b
